---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';
import { ExternalLink } from 'lucide-react';

const title = "Terms of Service | CertifiTrack";
const description = "Terms and conditions for using the CertifiTrack open-source COI document extraction tool.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="spacing-section bg-background border-b border-border">
    <div class="reading-width px-4 sm:px-6">
      
      {/* Header */}
      <div class="mb-10">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-1 text-caption text-muted-foreground mb-4 shadow-subtle">
          Terms & Conditions
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-h1 text-foreground spacing-heading">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-small text-muted-foreground">Last updated: August 2026</p>
      </div>

      {/* Intro Box */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface shadow-subtle mb-10 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-h3 text-foreground text-base font-semibold">Important Notice</h2>
        <p class="text-small text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          CertifiTrack is an automated open-source software tool for extracting data from insurance certificates. It does not provide legal, insurance underwriting, or compliance counsel. Always independently verify extracted data against source certificate documents.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Content Sections */}
      <div class="space-y-10 text-body">
        
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-h2 text-foreground text-xl">1. Description of Software</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            CertifiTrack provides automated document ingestion and data extraction for ACORD 25 Certificates of Insurance. The software parses uploaded PDF files or ZIP archives, extracts commercial liability policy fields, validates date formats, and compiles the results into a structured Excel (.xlsx) workbook.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-h2 text-foreground text-xl">2. No Insurance or Compliance Advice</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            CertifiTrack is NOT an insurance agency, broker, or legal compliance authority. The software does not determine insurance adequacy, verify policy active status with carriers, or guarantee that subcontractors meet specific contract requirements.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            You are solely responsible for reviewing and verifying all extracted policy numbers, expiration dates, and coverage limits before making operational, hiring, or compliance decisions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-h2 text-foreground text-xl">3. File Handling & Lifecycle</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Uploaded files are stored temporarily on the server purely to execute text extraction and date normalization. As soon as the output spreadsheet is generated or if an extraction error occurs, temporary files are immediately removed from disk. CertifiTrack does not retain permanent copies of your documents.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-h2 text-foreground text-xl">4. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            CertifiTrack is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            In no event shall the authors, maintainers, or contributors be liable for any claim, damages, or losses arising from the use of this software, errors in automated data extraction, or reliance on generated output files.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-h2 text-foreground text-xl">5. Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            You retain all ownership rights to the documents and data you process through CertifiTrack. The CertifiTrack codebase is open-source software accessible under its respective repository license.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 pt-6 border-t border-border">
          <h2 class="text-h2 text-foreground text-xl">6. Contact & Repository</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            For questions regarding these terms, issue reports, or open-source contributions:
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 pt-2">
            <a 
              href={siteConfig.socials.github} 
              target="_blank" 
              rel="noopener noreferrer" 
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-foreground hover:underline"
            >
              <span>GitHub Repository</span>
              <ExternalLink class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
            </a>
            <span class="hidden sm:inline text-muted-foreground">&bull;</span>
            <a 
              href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`} 
              class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground hover:underline"
            >
              {siteConfig.supportEmail}
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
